00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.520
Global cultures deeply ingrained in this

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.280
franchises route and a big part of what makes Jojo feel unique.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.680
Setting aside the countless music references in the names of the characters and stands,

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.540
let's take a look at some of these influences.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.300
Part 1: Phantom Blood starts off in 19th century Britain,

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.440
in the time of Jack the Ripper

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.680
with the heavy inclusion of vampires being somewhat of

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.700
a love letter to Bram Stoker's Dracula.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.300
Coming out during the late 80s,

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.700
it was nearer where stars like Stallone and Arnie War

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.400
everyday action stars on the big screen

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.720
which was a huge inspiration for bulky muscly designs that were a staple in these early days,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.640
along with the iconic fist of the North Star.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:29.800
[Arnie War]Who The Hell Are You?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.140
[Jonathan]Jonathan Joestar!

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:34.340
The early franchise can almost be viewed as the celebration of culture at the time.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:38.380
And this can truly be seen in Part 2: Battle Tendency, which switches us over to America

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:44.200
And it is here where the 80s culture and the over-the-top bravado of the action movies of the time get a chance to truly shine.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.420
(which it does)

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:50.400
Combined with more global influences, World War II, Nazis, and Villains heavily influenced by

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.120
Egyptian, Japanese and Roman statues of gods.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.000
All this leads to Stardust Crusaders,

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.520
where Araki fully embraces the global influence,

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.460
plotting a roadtrip style story inspired by

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.740
Jules Verne's Around The World in 80 Days,

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.800
taking our crew to all sorts of exotic places internationally

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.080
and with this flexibility of setting came the chance for

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.980
Araki's external influences to truly run wild .

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.180
His love for Western Horror was made even more evident,

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.100
with characters like Enya and Hanged Man.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.080
And other villains reminiscent of the premise you known cult horror flicks like

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.020
Nightmare on Elm Street and Child's Play

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.820
Hol Horse as a character was born from his love of Westerns

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:23.180
and hell, more importantly

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.900
Jotaro was specifically inspired by Clint Eastwood movies

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.060
with both the signature pose and even his catchpharse

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:31.980
being inspired by Eastwood's iconic images and attitudes in certain films.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:34.760
[Clint Eastwood] Go ahead, make my day.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.260
